  "implementation": [
    "Extend the existing immutable ReferenceInput with hover and locked-direction state. Reuse the common directed curve extraction, endpoint clamping and confirmed closed-length helpers, with usd-brep when enabled. Share D/Direction parsing with standalone SubCrv and OrientOnCrv.",
    "Locked open numeric lengths finish immediately. Free numeric and all closed numeric portions await confirmation; closed confirmation can choose either side. Opposite/same-side failures on locked open point input, Enter and zero length return to the parent reference picker, retaining the conic endpoints.",
    "Respect a locked backward closed portion by reversing the station order while retaining source traversal. Use the same stations for geometry and preview. Project trim picks without requiring an endpoint tangent.",
    "Route temporary Conic previews through the existing immutable-snapshot cache, retaining source orientation. Repeated frames reuse the same geometry; new hover, direction, length, source or availability changes invalidate or hide the preview. Do not add helper objects or document history.",
    "Extend the authored conic_command oracle recipe with hover actions and explicit surface-edge picks. Check that the authored local pick position lies on its named edge. Compare every complete result with the independent native command rather than importing native geometry into production.",
    "Drive public Rhino getters with managed UI expression delegates. A small adapter emitted from our own instructions overrides the documented MouseCallback.OnEndMouseMove; only an actual matching move in the owned viewport acknowledges hover. Deliver physical edge clicks only in the newly owned private window, and restore callbacks, timers, settings and views."
  ],
